# Aliases of BecomesFalse_no_ext_ref.mat: where it records a generated signal that
# no name ties to it. Format and rules: ReferenceResolver and Aliases in
# compiler/src/test/.../verification/engine/verification/reference.
#
# The reference model, CRML_test.ETL.BecomesFalse_no_ext, keeps c1 and c2 as
# synchronous Modelica clocks:
#   c1 = clockEvent1.y, from b1.y -> booleanToBoolean4_1 -> not4_1 -> event4ToEvent
#   c2 = clockEvent2.y, from b2.y -> booleanToBoolean4_2 -> not4_2 -> event4ToEvent1
# The result file names their partitions only _Clocks.BaseClock_<n>. BaseClock_0
# ticks at 5 s and 9 s, where b1 becomes false, and BaseClock_1 never ticks, as b2
# is constantly true (the behaviour BecomesFalse_no_ext.crml specifies), so
# BaseClock_0 is c1 and BaseClock_1 is c2.
#
# generated signal   reference signal                                  encoding
c1.out               _Clocks.BaseClock_0.SubClock_1.activationCount    COUNTER
c2.out               _Clocks.BaseClock_1.SubClock_1.activationCount    COUNTER
